.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates a Windows Named Pipe instance for use as an alternative
transport to Unix domain sockets.
The pipe path is:
.IP
.EX
\(rs\(rs.\(rspipe\(rsbash\-server\-<name>
.EE
.PP
The pipe is created with the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Security\f[R]: Owner\-only DACL via SDDL string
\f[CR]\(dqD:(A;;GA;;;OW)\(dq\f[R], which grants Generic All access
exclusively to the pipe owner.
This is equivalent to Unix socket permissions \f[CR]0600\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Mode\f[R]:
\f[CR]PIPE_TYPE_BYTE | PIPE_READMODE_BYTE | PIPE_WAIT\f[R] (byte\-mode,
synchronous).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]No overlapped I/O\f[R]: The pipe is created \f[B]without\f[R]
\f[CR]FILE_FLAG_OVERLAPPED\f[R].
This is intentional: after \f[CR]cygwin_attach_handle_to_fd()\f[R]
converts the HANDLE to a POSIX fd, Cygwin\(cqs
\f[CR]read()\f[R]/\f[CR]write()\f[R] use synchronous
\f[CR]ReadFile\f[R]/\f[CR]WriteFile\f[R], which is compatible with the
existing protocol code.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Instances\f[R]: \f[CR]PIPE_UNLIMITED_INSTANCES\f[R] allows multiple
concurrent pipe instances for parallel client connections.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Buffer sizes\f[R]: \f[CR]SERVER_MAX_LINE\f[R] (8192 bytes) for both
input and output buffers.
.PP
Named Pipes bypass Cygwin\(cqs AF_UNIX\-over\-TCP\-loopback emulation,
eliminating the \f[CR]SO_PEERCRED\f[R] handshake race condition that
affects Unix sockets on Cygwin.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]name\f[R] \(em Pipe name suffix.
Appended to \f[CR]\(rs\(rs.\(rspipe\(rsbash\-server\-\f[R] to form the
full pipe path.
Must not be NULL or empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a Win32 \f[CR]HANDLE\f[R] to the pipe instance on success.
.PP
Returns \f[CR]INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE\f[R] on error.
Error details are printed to stderr.
